WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.340
The Avengers aren't the only ones making a
huge comeback this year.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.240
Disney and Marvel Studios have made the unexpected
decision to re-hire James Gunn to finish what

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.950
he started with the Guardians of the Galaxy
series.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.620
What happened in the months since Gunn's firing
to make this unlikely triumph possible?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.920
To call James Gunn's firing in July 2018 "unexpected"
would be a bit of an understatement.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.019
Under Gunn's direction, the Guardians came
out of nowhere to become one of the most successful

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:31.289
series in the Marvel Cinematic Universe...
pretty impressive for a property that was

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:34.120
all but unknown before 2014.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.440
On top of the money the movies brought in,
they also earned rave reviews, making talking

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.140
trees and trash pandas beloved household names
for families across the world.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.310
"... you stupid raccoon."

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.060
"Don't call me a raccoon!"

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.120
But as Gunn's sudden firing seemed to demonstrate,
all of that success meant nothing in the face

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:52.570
of corporate mandate.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.480
The third Guardians movie was originally set
to begin filming in fall 2018, but was shut

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.789
down indefinitely after the controversial
decision was made to fire Gunn for provocative

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:02.879
past tweets.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:07.440
A few days after Disney's decision was made
public, the main cast of the franchise rebuked

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.990
the company with an extraordinary open letter
calling for Gunn to be reinstated.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.520
The remarkable show of support left many hoping
that the situation could be turned around.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.040
But publicly, the company was unswayed, and
it soon looked like Disney would rather scuttle

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.300
Volume 3 in its entirety than bring Gunn back.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:30.040
If many movies in the MCU feel like they're
designed by committee, it's mostly because…

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.650
well, they are.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:36.540
But Gunn's Guardians of the Galaxy movies
are often seen as being uniquely his, fusing

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.150
the out-there humor of his satirical movies
with a more Disney-approved, family-friendly

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:41.780
vibe.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.280
While we don't know what went on internally
in the wake of Gunn's firing, fans and commentators

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.860
stressed over the idea of someone else taking
over Gunn's job as director.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.100
How could a replacement for Gunn effectively
mimic his style?

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.770
And even if they could, wouldn't it just feel
kind of hollow?

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.340
Rumors were abundant of potential replacements
for the filmmaker, including Thor: Ragnarok

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.060
director Taika Waititi.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.690
But according to the Deadline report that
announced Gunn's reinstatement, all of this

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:10.810
chatter was only rumor, and Marvel Studios
never approached or considered any other filmmaker

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.720
to head up the delayed project.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:18.780
In the aftermath of James Gunn's firing, Drax
the Destroyer actor Dave Bautista went to

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.700
town on social media, sharing to anyone who
would listen that he would straight-up quit

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.310
his job if Marvel Studios declined to press
forward with Gunn's Vol. 3 script.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.260
The actor said in an interview with ShortList,

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.480
Whether Bautista had anything to do with it
or not, it was soon reported that Marvel and

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.870
Disney would indeed be moving forward with
Gunn's script.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.830
It seems likely that the studios were in a
tight bind regarding the screenplay.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:55.750
Guardians Vol. 2 clearly laid the groundwork
for future storylines in the Marvel cosmic,

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:00.010
such as the introduction of Adam Warlock,
presumably with the expectation that Gunn's

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.510
Vol. 3 script would follow up on them.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.890
After that script was written and incorporated
into the MCU's future, it may have been too

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.000
difficult to get rid of Gunn's screenplay
without compromising the series' house of

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.000
cards meta-plot.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.510
Plus, unless they completely threw out his
script and changed everything, it may have

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.950
been impossible to re-write Gunn's draft without
having to credit him anyway for laying the

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:21.940
groundwork.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:27.840
According to the Deadline report that broke
the story, Gunn's rehiring is not a new development,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.840
at least internally.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.630
The decision was apparently made months ago.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.760
In the aftermath of his firing, Gunn kept
silent, even as the reaction from fans got

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.010
louder and louder.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:41.709
The writer-director received an enormous amount
of public support, with one Change.org petition

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:45.560
calling for his re-hiring getting hundreds
of thousands of signatures.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.040
But despite the support, Gunn publicly accepted
Disney's decision which turned out to be the

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.120
right move.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.709
Apparently, Gunn's calm reaction to the controversy
helped convince Walt Disney Studios chairman

00:03:55.709 --> 00:03:58.790
Alan Horn that the company had made the wrong
call.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.340
Now, it looks like Gunn's refusal to burn
bridges has brought him the best of all possible

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.630
worlds... a relationship with DC and Marvel
Studios, and huge projects in the works for

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:09.340
both.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.500
In October, just three months after being
shown the door by Disney, Gunn surprisingly

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.560
loaded up his next project with rival studios
Warner Bros. and DC, being tapped to both

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.880
write and direct a follow-up to DC's Suicide
Squad.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.350
People's minds were blown so hard, you'd think
Harley Quinn went to town on them with a baseball

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.000
bat.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.560
Before long, many moviegoers were already
getting comfortable with the new status quo,

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.130
assuming Guardians of the Galaxy was done
for and getting weirdly excited about a Suicide

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.130
Squad 2.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.660
"We're gonna start having some real fun."

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.920
"Why don't we have some fun?"

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.020
But it turns out, whatever deal Gunn signed
with Warner Bros. wasn't an exclusive one,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.990
leaving him free to resume work on Vol. 3
when he's wrapped up with the Suicide Squad

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.980
sequel.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:56.880
One factor that may have made it easy to bring
Gunn back is just how good for business the

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.550
filmmaker has been for Disney.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.550
Together, the first two movies in the Guardians
of the Galaxy series earned a combined total

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:08.990
of over $1.6 billion and that's just the movie
money, not the cash raked in by toys, theme

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.230
park rides, and other properties associated
with the brand.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:16.680
In the short-term, Gunn's history of tasteless
jokes may have felt damaging enough to Disney

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.949
to justify the backlash that would come from
firing him.

00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:24.199
Somewhere along the way, that seems to have
changed, and now Disney and Marvel Studios

00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:29.180
are set to deliver not just a highly-anticipated
sequel, but one many had resigned to thinking

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.699
was never going to happen the way it was originally
intended.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.560
Apparently not even the Mouse House can say
no to another easy billion.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:42.840
James Gunn's unique aptitude for working with
Marvel hasn't gone unnoticed over the years,

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:46.780
with the once-fringe filmmaker being drawn
closer into the company's brain trust.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.080
At times, it's seemed possible that he could
one day take the whole thing over should producer

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.910
Kevin Feige step down.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.350
Feige himself has sung Gunn's praises in the
past, telling The Hollywood Reporter that

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:02.100
Gunn could, quote, "easily oversee additional
stories [in the MCU] beyond Vol. 3."

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.470
Now, we might really get to see all of that
unfold.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:09.870
After the news broke that Gunn had been re-hired
for Vol. 3, the writer-director shared a statement

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.480
on his Twitter page, writing,

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.580
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:29.120
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.760
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

